    <paragraph>Identify the Graph of each Equation as a Circle, Parabola, Ellipse, or Hyperbola</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, identify the type of graph.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="174" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$x = -y^{2} - 2y + 3$$ ⓑ $$9y^{2} - x^{2} + 18y - 4x - 4 = 0$$ ⓒ $$9x^{2} + 25y^{2} = 225$$ ⓓ $$x^{2} + y^{2} - 4x + 10y - 7 = 0$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="175" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$x = -2y^{2} - 12y - 16$$ ⓑ $$x^{2} + y^{2} = 9$$ ⓒ $$16x^{2} - 4y^{2} + 64x - 24y - 36 = 0$$ ⓓ $$16x^{2} + 36y^{2} = 576$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ parabola ⓑ circle ⓒ hyperbola ⓓ ellipse</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
